\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Elicitation and acquisition}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{post-training}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{A measured gain is \strong{elicitation} when training or inference places
more probability on successful behaviour already represented in the starting
policy's effective support. A gain is \strong{acquisition} when independently
validated successful behaviour becomes available where the declared starting
procedure had negligible support, or when the behaviour transfers under a
prespecified test that the starting procedure failed.}

\p{These are FTIP working definitions. They sharpen a distinction investigated
empirically by \citef{liu2025understanding} and \citef{yue2025does}. Those
papers compare base and RL-trained reasoning models, but no finite experiment
can establish exact zero support for an unrestricted policy. For that reason,
the definition refers to effective support under a declared procedure.}

\p{The two terms describe an experimental contrast rather than an exhaustive
partition of learning. A result may combine both. Later trees define support,
evaluation budgets, and an acquisition witness so that the contrast can be
tested without relying on a verbal judgment about a generated trace.}
